From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ole32: objref monikers, class and file icons, registered formats, link query, enumerator Skip/Clone

- OBJREF monikers (CreateObjrefMoniker) were half there: Save, size,
  binding, reduction, composition, the display name and its parsing were
  stubs. Save writes the object's marshalled reference (Load reads it
  back and unmarshals it); the display name is "objref:" + that
  reference in base64 + ":", which MkParseDisplayName reads back to the
  object; BindToObject and BindToStorage give the object; an anti
  moniker composed on the right takes the moniker away. Wine's moniker
  test no longer marks these as todo.
- OleGetIconOfClass (a stub) makes the class's icon picture: the icon
  from the class's DefaultIcon, labelled with the label given or its
  short type name (AuxUserType\2) or "Document". OleGetIconOfFile (a
  stub) does it for a file: the shell's icon for it, labelled with the
  file's name.
- OleRegEnumFormatEtc (a stub) enumerates the formats a class registers
  under DataFormats\GetSet for the direction asked
  (REGDB_E_KEYMISSING when there are none).
- OleQueryLinkFromData (a stub that said no) answers whether the data
  offers a "Link Source".
- OleCreateFromDataEx caches the formats asked for, fills the cache from
  the data and advises the sink (FIXME: init cache).
- OleInitializeWOW (a stub that did nothing) initializes OLE.
- The property and property set enumerators' Skip and Clone (FIXMEs);
  a skip of none ends a property set enumeration, as Windows does
  (Wine's stg_prop test's todos now pass and are no longer marked).

Wine's ole32 moniker (19 failures before, none now), ole2, stg_prop,
propvariant and clipboard tests: no failures.

Gate: test/ole32misc-gate.sh (Xvfb, test/ole32misc-probe.c).
Mutants SG_MUTANT_NO_OBJREF_SAVE (ole32/pointermoniker.c),
SG_MUTANT_NO_REG_FORMATS (ole32/ole2stubs.c).
